<p><br></p>
<h3 id=3D"Employeeaccesscurrentstaterequestfulfillment-NetRepapplication">N=
etRep application</h3>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"20183d30-b0e6-409e-b687-13eb2b6a4380">In addition, when r=
equesting an access to <span>NetRep (App id: 2213), the requestor&nbsp;</sp=
an>
  <ul>
   <li><span>Can select trade access, by trading products (e.g. equity, opt=
ions, fixed income)</span></li>
   <li><span>Can select view-only access</span></li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4ea13775-c278-46a3-8810-c29d7a4db566">There are three dif=
ferent versions of NetRep:&nbsp;=20
  <ul>
   <li>
    <p>HSW - IAVM only</p></li>
   <li>
    <p><span>NBC - NetRep2</span></p></li>
   <li>
    <p>NPM - NetRep PM</p></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"da7a278e-b9da-44fd-ab83-10ffd10c839a"><span>Creating a ne=
w NetRep id implies creating a new OSS id, but the OSS id will not be share=
d to the requestor.</span>
  <ul>
   <li><span>OSS id will not be shared among users even though they work fo=
r the same firm</span></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"fa63c092-a9ff-4d06-83ec-b6a6d84cc997">The max. number of =
RR codes can be assigned to an id is 102. Alternatively, use branch code (t=
he first 2-letter of RR code)</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"4b14ee8b-5c6a-4968-9a24-c9011f3737c3"><span>These are the=
 3 popular &nbsp;datagroup in Secured zone:</span>
  <ul>
   <li><span>NBDB =3D FICEBN<br></span></li>
   <li><span>NBF =3D FIFBNNBF<br></span></li>
   <li><span>NBCN =3D FICORNET</span></li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<h3 id=3D"Employeeaccesscurrentstaterequestfulfillment-DWHapplications"><sp=
an>DWH applications</span></h3>
<p><span>Current process flow: <a href=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/spaces/NDSKW/=
pages/1846584538/Data+Solutions+WebApps-Access+Request" rel=3D"nofollow">Da=
ta Solutions WebApps-Access Request - NBIN Data Services team - Confluence<=
/a></span></p>
<ul>
 <li><span>Managers will go to IIQ (<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http=
s://iiq.bnc.ca/identityiq/home.jsf" rel=3D"nofollow">https://iiq.bnc.ca/ide=
ntityiq/home.jsf</a>) and request DWH app access (1 to 12 apps)&nbsp;</span=
><span>&nbsp;</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"5d1dad2f-01cb-490d-8225-b279fcebfd68"><span>The process w=
ould create a new Okta user account (in NBC tenant) with the required DWH u=
ser groups, however, the user configuration will have to be entered to Comp=
ass manually</span></li>
 <li><span>Current pain points:</span>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"f281c3d7-d39f-4ed8-a6fc-5e6af58553be"><span>Managers wi=
ll have to submit the app access request one per app, though most of the ti=
me only 1 or 2 are eligible</span></li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"03534e6a-1167-4395-8f71-5ec924d5f67e"><span>The DWH use=
r admin needs to request a list of new users from Okta admin group on an ad=
-hoc basis, which sometimes take up to weeks</span></li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"6b411f57-14ce-4b2b-bc6b-9d0fefff7af0">The DWH user admi=
n will have to log in Compass, enter the user configuration including the O=
kta id manually, which is time-consuming and error-prone&nbsp;</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"0e26fa03-a26e-4afc-9c8e-1734bde3b9ab">There is no DWH u=
ser deactivation capability provided to DWH user admin; no departed employe=
es have ever been offboarded, causing data integrity issue and security con=
cern</li>
   <li data-uuid=3D"8297ba12-cdb4-4f10-bc9b-68dd50c24267">The DWH user grou=
ps and resources are persisted in Compass db, increasing the maintenance ef=
forts and overlooking by FUM change impacts&nbsp;</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
